      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a33f59b7f2ea83fad4a5ecd|full_name}: Yeah... my broader idea for a scriptable advanced shields/hider/performance override (which I've mentioned once in a dev update comment and also talked to Tupper about in passing) does specifically include being able to parametrically choose whether to show someone's normal avatar, fallback, robot, diamond, or nothing at all (and turn on/off specific avatar features eg shaders or lights with configurable thresholds), for precisely the reason that sometimes people don't like partying with a bunch of robots but still want high shields.\n\nTo not get too far off track though, I didn't particularly intend for a list of hidden users to appear in that concept, since I generally believe that undoing a player moderation should be easy, and if you've baked the person's ID into a script then it becomes hard to change your mind about hiding them... and the idea for this request is specifically about when you hide a particular user, because sometimes the reason you want to hide them isn't solved by replacing them with a robot (eg they're in a quite large avatar and standing in the middle of a small dance floor).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-05-30T22:45:07.642Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently if you hide a user, you still see the robot. This is good in cases where the avatar has annoying shaders (the majority of the time I feel like hiding anyone), but doesn't help if they are obstructing you (intentionally or not). I don't like blocking people because of the bidirectionality of blocks, but if someone is in an overly large avatar or otherwise getting in my way I still want to be able to hide them in a way that meaningfully remedies the situation for me.\n\nSo ideally, you would be able to set a toggle when hiding a user, which would indicate whether you want to see the robot or a transparent diamond (a la hiding-by-distance).",
